+// node, which may be a *DurationExpr or a *NumberLiteral. A non-nil parenPos
+// means the operand was parenthesised, with parenPos being the position of the
+// opening parenthesis; the parentheses are then preserved on the result.
+func (p *parser) applyUnaryOpToDurationExpr(op Item, expr Node, parenPos *posrange.Pos) Node {
